@startuml
title Building the proof off-chain, before the transaction is submitted

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam activityBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
skinparam activityBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam activityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam activityDiamondBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #F7FAFF
skinparam noteBorderColor #4A78B5

start
:Collect the parties: the inline stake
credential of every input and output
carrying the security token;<<#EEF5FF>>
note right
  A party is a CREDENTIAL, not an
  address and not a UTxO. A key and
  a script sharing a hash are two
  different parties.
end note

:Read the denylist from an indexer:
every UTxO at the denylist address
holding a list-policy NFT;<<#EEF5FF>>
:Decode each node - key from the asset
name after the 4-byte "Node" prefix,
link from the inline datum;<<#EEF5FF>>

repeat :Take the next party hash h;<<#EEF5FF>>
  if (A node keyed exactly at h?) then (yes)
    :STOP - this party is sanctioned.
    No covering node exists, so the
    transaction cannot be built;<<#FDEEEE>>
    stop
  else (no)
    :Select the node P with
    P.key < h < P.link;<<#EEF5FF>>
    :Add P to reference_inputs
    (never as a spend);<<#EEF5FF>>
  endif
repeat while (More parties?) is (yes) not (no)

:Order the action list to match the order
the validator will derive the parties;<<#EEF5FF>>
note right
  Actions are matched POSITIONALLY.
  Inputs are canonically sorted by the
  ledger before any script runs, so the
  sender order is not the order you
  listed them. Output order is yours.
end note

:Keep parties citing the same covering
node adjacent, so the node is
authenticated once per run;<<#EEF5FF>>
:Attach each action: the covering-node
index into reference_inputs, plus a KYC
proof when the flag is set;<<#EEF5FF>>
:Submit;<<#EAF6F0>>
stop
@enduml
